---
import BlogLayout from '../../layouts/BlogLayout.astro';

const frontmatter = {
  title: 'Hello, World — New Site, New Stack',
  description: 'Rebuilding prawegko.dev with Astro, deployed on S3/CloudFront with OIDC CI/CD.',
  date: new Date('2026-09-30T12:00:00'),
  tags: ['Meta', 'Astro', 'AWS', 'Cloud'],
};
---

<BlogLayout frontmatter={frontmatter}>
  <p>Welcome to the new prawegko.dev. This site is built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a>, a modern static site generator that produces fast, lightweight websites by default.</p>

  <h2>Why Astro?</h2>
  <p>After running on NextJS + Vercel for a while, I wanted to try a different deployment approach:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Static by default</strong> — Astro ships zero JavaScript unless you need it</li>
    <li><strong>Content Collections</strong> — native MDX support with typed frontmatter</li>
    <li><strong>Cloud-native deployment</strong> — S3 + CloudFront with OIDC-based GitHub Actions CI/CD</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The Stack</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Layer</th><th>Choice</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Framework</td><td>Astro 7 + TypeScript</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Styling</td><td>Tailwind CSS v4</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Hosting</td><td>AWS S3 (prawegko.dev bucket)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>CDN</td><td>CloudFront</td></tr>
    <tr><td>CI/CD</td><td>GitHub Actions with OIDC role deploy</td></tr>
    <tr><td>DNS</td><td>Vercel DNS → CloudFront</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>The Workflow</h2>
  <pre><code>git push origin main
  -> npm ci
  -> npm run build
  -> aws s3 sync dist/ s3://prawegko.dev --delete
  -> aws cloudfront create-invalidation ...</code></pre>
  <p>All authenticated through GitHub's OIDC provider — no long-lived AWS keys needed.</p>
  <p>More posts coming soon. Stay tuned.</p>
</BlogLayout>
